---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import { felix, organization } from '../data/felix';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const calLink = 'https://cal.com/nomadtaxhelp/clarity-call';

const allPosts = await getCollection('posts', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const latestPosts = allPosts
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.publishDate.getTime() - a.data.publishDate.getTime())
  .slice(0, 4);

const expertise = [
  { label: 'Paraguay tax residency', href: '/category/paraguay' },
  { label: 'European tax exits', href: '/category/tax-residency' },
  { label: 'Crypto realisation strategy', href: '/posts/paraguay-crypto-tax-residency' },
  { label: 'Portugal NHR alternatives', href: '/posts/portugal-nhr-replacement-2026' },
  { label: 'Tax-residency glossary', href: '/glossary' },
];

// AboutPage + Person JSON-LD — gives LLMs and search engines a canonical
// person entity to disambiguate "Felix Yanez-Bowker" against.
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'AboutPage',
      '@id': 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/about#aboutpage',
      url: 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/about',
      name: 'About Felix Yanez-Bowker',
      mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/about#felix' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/about#felix',
      name: felix.name,
      givenName: felix.givenName,
      familyName: felix.familyName,
      jobTitle: felix.jobTitle,
      description: felix.description,
      url: felix.url,
      image: felix.image,
      email: felix.email,
      knowsAbout: felix.knowsAbout,
      sameAs: felix.sameAs,
      worksFor: { '@id': 'https://nomadtaxhelp.com/#organization' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: 'https://blog.nomadtaxhelp.com/about' },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | NomadTaxHelp Blog"
  description="Felix Yanez-Bowker is the co-founder of NomadTaxHelp. He writes about tax residency, US LLCs, and how nomads can build clean, defensible cross-border setups."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-[680px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-6 mb-8">
      <a
        href="/images/felix.png"
        data-lightbox="/images/felix.png"
        data-lightbox-alt="Felix Yanez-Bowker"
        class="shrink-0 no-underline"
        aria-label="View larger photo of Felix"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/felix.png"
          alt="Felix Yanez-Bowker"
          width="200"
          height="200"
          class="w-[200px] h-[200px] rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-teal-900/10 shadow-sm"
        />
      </a>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-4">
          Hi, I'm Felix <span aria-hidden="true">👋</span><br />
          I help nomads with their tax setup
        </h1>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felix-yanez-bowker-b23270252/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer me"
            class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-teal-900/20 text-teal-900 no-underline hover:border-amber-600 hover:text-amber-600 transition-colors"
          >
            LinkedIn &rarr;
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://felixyanez.substack.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer me"
            class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-teal-900/20 text-teal-900 no-underline hover:border-amber-600 hover:text-amber-600 transition-colors"
          >
            Personal blog &rarr;
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://fascinated-princess-801.notion.site/About-Me-54522f72ef6a470aa87711bb889cd30c"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer me"
            class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-teal-900/20 text-teal-900 no-underline hover:border-amber-600 hover:text-amber-600 transition-colors"
          >
            Personal site &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm a co-founder of <a href="https://nomadtaxhelp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NomadTaxHelp</a> &mdash; where we help digital nomads &amp; remote entrepreneurs build legal, low-tax setups that are designed to practically work for their nuanced lifestyle.
      </p>

      <p>
        I started this because I went through the same maze myself: trying to work out which residency to take, how to exit cleanly, what would actually protect me, and which advisers were worth listening to. Most of what I read was either too technical, too generic, or too obviously trying to sell me something. I spent a lot of time, a lot of money, and sat with a lot of stress when dealing with the perpetual question looming over me: "what the hell do I do with my taxes!?"
      </p>

      <p>
        Now, I'm based between Andorra, Spain, Indonesia and wherever the snow is good. I'm British, 29, and I've been location-independent for the better part of a decade. Before NomadTaxHelp I spent six years at a hedge fund, <a href="http://168trading.fund" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">168trading.fund</a>, and I still write a separate blog on geopolitics, demographics, and decentralisation called <a href="https://felixyanez.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me"><em>The Curious Cat</em></a>. Tax residency for nomads sits at the intersection of a lot of the things I find genuinely interesting: how individuals navigate states, how money flows across borders, and what it actually takes to live a free life in 2026; and ultimately, how to become a <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/2708480-the-sovereign-individual" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sovereign Individual</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What NTH does</h2>

      <p>
        NomadTaxHelp's core service is end-to-end Paraguay residency setup, paired with optional US LLC formation. Paraguay gives you legal 0% tax on foreign-source income through a 3-day setup visit, with low ongoing presence requirements. We handle the documents, the in-country logistics, the tax number, the residency certificate, and the US LLC if you want it. We've built this with a partner team in Asunci&oacute;n who handle everything on the ground. Our clients have a 100% approval rate.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you want to know more about the service itself, the <a href="https://nomadtaxhelp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">main site</a> covers it. If you want to talk it through directly, <a href={calLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">book a free 20-minute clarity call</a> and I'll map your situation.
      </p>

      <h2>What I write about</h2>

      <p>
        The blog covers the full nomad tax stack — exiting your home country cleanly, picking a defensible new residency, structuring your income, and proving everything to a tax authority that asks. Here are the threads I keep pulling on:
      </p>

      <ul>
        {expertise.map((e) => (
          <li><a href={e.href}>{e.label}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Latest guides</h2>

      <ul>
        {latestPosts.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/posts/${p.data.slug}`}>{p.data.title}</a>
            <span class="text-sm text-gray-600"> &middot; <time datetime={p.data.publishDate.toISOString()}>
              {p.data.publishDate.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}
            </time></span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>What NTH isn't</h2>

      <p>
        NomadTaxHelp is not a tax adviser or a legal adviser. We don't file your taxes, we don't draft contracts, and we don't give you formal legal opinions. We coordinate with licensed partners who do. Everything on this blog is educational. For anything specific to your situation, confirm with a professional in the relevant jurisdiction before you act on it. That's not a disclaimer for legal cover, it's how this stuff actually works: tax law is local, and your specifics matter.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Book a free clarity call: <a href={calLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cal.com/nomadtaxhelp/clarity-call</a></li>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@nomadtaxhelp.com">hello@nomadtaxhelp.com</a></li>
        <li>Instagram: <a href="https://instagram.com/nomadtaxhelp_" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@nomadtaxhelp_</a></li>
        <li>LinkedIn: <a href={felix.sameAs[0]} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me">linkedin.com/in/felix-yanez-bowker</a></li>
        <li>Personal blog (Substack): <a href={felix.sameAs[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer me">felixyanez.substack.com</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
